#
# The inference slice carries NO hand-authored closed-world shapes.
#
# Under equivalence-before-deletion (design/LOGIC-VALIDATION.md), every closed-world
# well-formedness obligation of this slice is now authored in the canon and reproduced by the
# projector (generated/shapes/validation-shapes.ttl and generated/shapes/constraint-shapes.ttl):
#
#   * InferenceCommitment, Correspondence, Analogy, Argument, ArgumentEvaluation, PremiseUse and
#     InferenceApplication — cardinality / class / datatype obligations authored as OWL restrictions
#     in module.ttl.
#   * Attack and Support — the role-filler cardinalities and the range disjunctions
#     (gmeow:attackTarget over PremiseUse/InferenceApplication/StandpointClaim, gmeow:supportSource
#     over Argument/StandpointClaim) authored as OWL restrictions (owl:cardinality + owl:allValuesFrom
#     over owl:unionOf → sh:or in validation-shapes.ttl).
#   * The abductive gmeow:InferenceCommitment obligations (mode = modeAbduction: an explanandum and a
#     candidate hypothesis) authored as a value-keyed general class axiom
#     ([ owl:onProperty gmeow:inferenceModeOf ; owl:hasValue gmeow:modeAbduction ] ⊑ …) → a value-keyed
#     sh:SPARQLTarget shape.
#   * The cross-node conflict discipline — premise ≠ conclusion, competesWith irreflexivity, no
#     self-attack / self-support, kind ↔ target agreement (undermine→PremiseUse, undercut→
#     InferenceApplication, rebut→StandpointClaim), and no argument-component self-attack — authored as
#     logic: FOL axioms (RelatumDistinctnessAssertion, PropertyCharacteristicAssertion,
#     ConditionalRangeAssertion, RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion) in slices/grounding/logic/module.ttl
#     → sh:SPARQLConstraint node shapes in constraint-shapes.ttl, each carrying logic:formalizes.
#
# Their former hand-authored blocks were deleted once `gmeow-dev shape-equivalence --path
# slices/core/inference` proved the projection reproduces every covered fragment and the residue is
# grounded in the canon.
